---
// The deep-dive editorial shell: the grid that the three article routes lay
// their four regions out on — header, contents, body, end matter.
// Transcribed from specs/design/prototypes/tooling-deepdive.html.
//
// One column by default. The second column only exists when the article
// earned a contents list (>=3 h2s, specs/pages/writing-article.md §2.2), and
// only from 900px up; below that the contents render inline, above the body,
// in their source position.
//
// Every directional property binds logically (specs/content-model.md §5
// rule 4), so the contents column lands on the right under dir="rtl" with no
// special case. `min-[900px]:gap-x-12` is the COLUMN gap and it flips with
// the axis; `gap-y-0` is the row gap and does not. A single-value gap utility
// in place of the pair would put 48px between every region as well, which is
// not what the prototype does.
//
// ── where the placement rules went ────────────────────────────────────────
//
// The stylesheet expressed this as `.with-contents > .article-header` and
// three siblings: a CHILD styled from a class on its PARENT. There is no
// utility for that, and the parent-state variants are the wrong tool anyway —
// the templates already compute `hasContents` before they render anything, so
// the flag is passed to each region and each region carries its own placement.
// The condition stays where it was decided instead of being re-derived from
// the DOM.
//
// The four placements, so the whole layout is readable in one place even
// though the utilities live on four elements:
//
//   header        both columns, row 1   ArticleHeader.astro
//   contents      column 1, row 2       Contents.astro (always placed — the
//                                       component only renders when there IS
//                                       a contents list, so the condition is
//                                       already spent by the time it mounts)
//   body          column 2, row 2       the three article templates, on the
//                                       <article class="article-body"> that
//                                       wraps the rendered MDX
//   end matter    column 2, row 3       EndMatter.astro
//
// The body is the one region with no component of its own. `article-body` is
// a frozen class name (tests/e2e/rtl.spec.ts) and its prose rules stay in
// article.css, because they style markdown-generated elements that carry no
// class attribute. Placement is safe to add on top of it: grid-column-start
// and grid-row-start are disjoint from the two properties that rule set owns
// on the element itself (max-inline-size, and the margin it gives its
// children). Checked, not assumed — a utility that touched margin there would
// land in the same layer as `.article-body > * + *` and the cascade would
// stop being decided by source order.

interface Props {
  /** Whether this article earned a contents list — the second column exists only then. */
  hasContents: boolean;
}

const { hasContents } = Astro.props;
---

<div
  class:list={[
    'grid grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)] gap-y-0',
    hasContents && 'min-[900px]:grid-cols-[200px_minmax(0,1fr)] min-[900px]:gap-x-12',
  ]}
>
  <slot />
</div>
